---
name: "Solutions"
title: "Solutions: LitLife™ genetic test kits | Lightening Lives"
description: "LitLife™ kits for sickle cell anaemia, sickle-beta, beta and alpha thalassaemia and SMA, from a dried blood spot. Coagulation and pharmacogenomics in development; new tests on request."
label: Solutions
h1: 'Kits we have developed. <span class="h-mark">Solutions for a wide range of diagnostic needs.</span>'
lead: "Five LitLife™ kits for inherited blood and muscle disorders, each reading mutations from a dried blood spot, and the next test built on request."
proof:
  - { icon: "badge-check", text: "ICMR approved" }
  - { icon: "award", text: "Patents granted in India and Japan" }
  - { icon: "map-pin", text: "15 sites, 9 states and Delhi" }
notice: true
closing:
  h2: 'Start with the condition <span class="h-mark">your programme needs.</span>'
  body: "Who will be tested, roughly how many, and where. We reply with how we would approach it."
  solid: { text: "Talk to our scientific team", href: "/contact/" }
  line: { text: "Partner with us", href: "/partners/" }
---
{#- Solutions (content file 5.3), since 25 October 2026 the user's catalogue grid, grouped by family:
    the kits we have developed, each a card with its box in 3D (it turns as the pointer moves over it;
    src/js/kits/viewer.js), its condition, its key features and "Read more" to its place on a test page;
    DMD and LGMD as cards that ask us; Develop a test with us (#develop, the page's main ask); what is
    under development; and Beyond the kits, what still holds of the old Services page, each item
    leading to the Partners page. The kits come from src/site/_data/kits.json. The jump links under
    the opening are the page's navigation. -#}
{%- set arrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 6h15M11 1l5 5-5 5"/></svg>' %}
{%- from "picture.njk" import picture with context %}
{%- from "faq.njk" import faq %}
<script type="module" src="/assets/js/site-kits.js"></script>

  <!-- The page's navigation: every kit, then the other two ways in; and what every kit shares -->
  <section id="kits" class="section on-mist kit-nav" aria-label="Kits on this page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ul class="kit-jumps">
        {%- for family in kits.families %}{% for kit in family.kits %}
        <li><a class="kit-jump" href="#{{ kit.id }}">{{ picture(kit.image, "", "3.5rem", { class: "kit-jump-img" }) }}<span><b>{{ kit.short }}</b><small>{{ kit.condition }}</small></span></a></li>
        {%- endfor %}{% endfor %}
        <li><a class="kit-jump kit-jump-plain" href="#develop"><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "plus" %}</span><span><b>Develop a test</b><small>Propose a condition</small></span></a></li>
        <li><a class="kit-jump kit-jump-plain" href="#in-development"><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "hourglass" %}</span><span><b>Under development</b><small>Two new families</small></span></a></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="kit-shared">
        <li>{% icon "droplet" %}<span>A dried blood spot</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "thermometer" %}<span>Room temperature transport</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "flask-conical" %}<span>No DNA extraction</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "microscope" %}<span>Standard PCR equipment</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- for family in kits.families %}
  <!-- {{ family.name }} -->
  <section id="{{ family.id }}" class="section{{ ' bg-paper' if loop.first }}" aria-labelledby="{{ family.id }}-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="{{ family.id }}-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7"><span class="family-icon icon-tile">{% icon family.icon %}</span>{{ family.name }}. <span class="h-mark">{{ family.sub }}.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">{{ family.lead }}</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="kit-grid mt-12">
        {%- for kit in family.kits %}
        <li id="{{ kit.id }}" class="kit-card">
          <div class="kit-stage" data-kit3d="{{ kit.model | dump }}" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="{{ kit.code }} box, in 3D. Drag to turn it, or use the arrow keys.">
            {{ picture(kit.image, kit.alt, "(min-width: 72rem) 22vw, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw", { class: "kit-img" }) }}
            <span class="kit-hint" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "rotate-3d" %}Drag to turn</span>
          </div>
          <a class="kit-link" href="{{ kit.href }}">
            <span class="kit-body">
              <span class="kit-condition">{{ kit.condition }}</span>
              <span class="kit-name" id="{{ kit.id }}-name">{{ kit.code }}</span>
              <span class="kit-features">
                {%- for f in kit.features %}
                <span>{% icon "circle-check-big" %}{{ f }}</span>
                {%- endfor %}
              </span>
              <span class="kit-more">Read more {% icon "arrow-right" %}</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- for ask in family.ask %}
        <li id="{{ ask.id }}" class="kit-card kit-ask">
          <a class="kit-link" href="/contact/">
            <span class="kit-body">
              <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "message-circle" %}</span>
              <span class="kit-condition">Molecular diagnosis available</span>
              <span class="kit-name">{{ ask.condition }}</span>
              <span class="kit-line">{{ ask.line }}</span>
              <span class="kit-more">Talk to us {% icon "arrow-right" %}</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- if family.also %}
      <p class="kit-also">{% icon "plus" %}<span>{{ family.also.text }} {% for l in family.also.links %}<a class="link" href="{{ l.href }}">{{ l.text }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span></p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  <!-- Develop a test with us: the page's main ask -->
  <section id="develop" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="develop-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="develop-band">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
          <h2 id="develop-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Develop a test with us. <span class="h-mark">Propose a condition.</span></h2>
          <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Every LitLife™ test began with a programme's need. If yours needs a test that doesn't exist, our scientists can develop and validate it.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="start-steps start-five mt-10">
          <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "message-circle" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">1</span> Brief</h3><p>You tell us the condition, the population and the setting.</p></li>
          <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "search" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">2</span> Feasibility</h3><p>Our scientists assess the genetics and the method.</p></li>
          <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "dna" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">3</span> Development</h3><p>We design and optimise the test.</p></li>
          <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "clipboard-check" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">4</span> Validation</h3><p>We validate it against reference methods on real samples.</p></li>
          <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "graduation-cap" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">5</span> Rollout</h3><p>Training, supply and support for your programme.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="audience-act">
          <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/contact/">Propose a condition</a>
          <span class="develop-note">A condition common in one community, a mutation profile specific to a region, or a format no one makes.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Under development -->
  <section id="in-development" class="section" aria-labelledby="in-development-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="in-development-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Under development. <span class="h-mark">The next two families.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Want early access, or to take part in validation? <a class="lead-link" href="/contact/">Tell us</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="dev-cards mt-12">
        <li>
          <span class="dev-tag">{% icon "hourglass" %}Under development</span>
          <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "droplets" %}</span>
          <h3>Blood coagulation panel</h3>
          <p>Genetic testing for inherited bleeding disorders such as haemophilia A and B. The panel will confirm a diagnosis, identify carriers and support family counselling.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="dev-tag">{% icon "hourglass" %}Under development</span>
          <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "pill" %}</span>
          <h3>Pharmacogenomics</h3>
          <p>Testing for the genetic differences that change how a person responds to a medicine, so that the drug and the dose can be chosen for the person.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beyond the kits: what still holds of the old Services page, each to the Partners page -->
  <section id="beyond" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="beyond-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="beyond-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Beyond the kits. <span class="h-mark">What we bring to a programme.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">A kit is the middle of the work. Around it, we help programmes and laboratories run it well.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="beyond mt-12">
        <li><a href="/partners/#programmes"><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "users" %}</span><b>Testing programmes</b><span>Screening for patients, carriers and newborns, and custom panels for a community.</span><span class="kit-more">For programmes {% icon "arrow-right" %}</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/partners/#funders"><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "megaphone" %}</span><b>Awareness and counselling</b><span>Screening and awareness camps, and genetic counselling for families.</span><span class="kit-more">For funders {% icon "arrow-right" %}</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/partners/#laboratories"><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "graduation-cap" %}</span><b>Training</b><span>Hands-on workshops for laboratory staff and health workers.</span><span class="kit-more">For laboratories {% icon "arrow-right" %}</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/partners/#laboratories"><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "microscope" %}</span><b>Laboratory set-up and consultancy</b><span>Setting up a molecular laboratory, and planning a programme or a grant.</span><span class="kit-more">For laboratories {% icon "arrow-right" %}</span></a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Questions we are asked -->
  <section id="faq" class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <div class="wrap grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <h2 id="faq-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-5">Questions <span class="h-mark">we are asked.</span></h2>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        {{ faq([
          { q: "Do you test individuals?", a: "No. We work with hospitals, laboratories, clinicians, NGOs, CSR funders and government health programmes. If you are looking for a test for yourself or your family, please speak to your doctor or visit your nearest government health facility." },
          { q: "What does our laboratory need to run the kits?", a: "A thermal cycler, a gel electrophoresis tank and a punch, a bench, and staff who have run PCR or have been trained. We help set the method up and train your staff." },
          { q: "How do samples reach the laboratory?", a: "On the card, at room temperature, by ordinary courier or post. No cold chain." },
          { q: "Are the kits approved?", a: "LitLife™-SCA, our sickle cell kit, is approved by ICMR. The technology behind our kits is patented in India and Japan." },
          { q: "Can you develop a test for a condition that isn't listed?", a: "Yes. Each test we have developed began with an institution that needed it. Tell us the condition and the setting, and we take it from there." }
        ]) }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
